# Unclogme Lovable handoff — Sandbox credential template
#
# Get the actual values from Fred (DM, never paste in shared channels).
# Lovable manages secrets via its Project Settings → Environment Variables UI;
# you don't usually need a literal .env file. This is a template showing the
# variable names Lovable uses.
#
# The Sandbox is a separate Supabase project (NOT a branch of Main). It's a
# full clone of Unclogme's production data — read everything, write anything.
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# Sandbox: "Unclogme - Sandbox" — created 2026-04-30
# Project ref: ubtlwpcyntelgbykdatn
# ============================================================================
# Lovable's "Connect Supabase" wizard uses SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.
SUPABASE_URL=https://ubtlwpcyntelgbykdatn.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...   # ← Get from Fred via DM. Public, RLS-gated. Safe in browser code.

# Server-side admin key. ONLY use in Edge Functions or scheduled jobs.
# Never embed in client-side code, never commit to git.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...   # ← Get from Fred. Bypasses RLS. Treat as a secret.

# ============================================================================
# Production storage (public-read, no auth needed).
# ============================================================================
# Don't change this — your Sandbox apps fetch photos from Main DB's storage,
# not from the Sandbox's own bucket. Saves duplicating ~12GB of photos.
# In React/Lovable code, build photo URLs as:
#   `${VITE_PRODUCTION_STORAGE_BASE}/GT%20-%20Visits%20Images/${storage_path}`
VITE_PRODUCTION_STORAGE_BASE=https://wbasvhvvismukaqdnouk.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public
